  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 1136 AM MST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\nGood agreement through the extended period between the\ndeterministic and ensemble guidance. The GFS has come more into\nline with the ECMWF and ensemble guidance with the mid week\nupper trough.\n\nTuesday through Saturday...overall, high pressure will continue\nto dominate southern Colorado through the next several days.\nThis will keep temperatures mainly in the 60s to near 70 across\nthe Plains, and 50s over the San Luis Valley. Overnight lows\nwill fall into the 30s for the Plains, and 20s for the San Luis\nValley. The upper trough forecast for mid week will pass well\nnorth and east, however, it will send a cold front across the\nPlains by Wednesday. This frontal boundary will be dry, and \nonly bring a brief cool down Wednesday afternoon by about 5-8 \ndegrees.\n\nBy next weekend, flow turns southwesterly and the upper ridge\nshifting east. A few showers could be possible along the\nContinental Divide next Saturday afternoon.",
